## Original Content
The primary runoff in South Carolina between Sen. Darline Graham and Rep. Ralph Norman is another test of President Trump's influence. He's backing Darline, sister of the late Sen. Lindsey Graham.

## Summary
The article discusses a primary runoff election in South Carolina for the U.S. Senate between Sen. Darline Graham and Rep. Ralph Norman. President Trump's endorsement of Darline Graham is highlighted as a test of his political influence. It notes that Darline Graham is the sister of the late Sen. Lindsey Graham.

## Key Points
- The primary runoff is for the U.S. Senate in South Carolina.
- Candidates are Sen. Darline Graham and Rep. Ralph Norman.
- President Trump is endorsing Darline Graham.
- This endorsement is seen as a test of Trump's influence.
- Darline Graham is related to the late Sen. Lindsey Graham.


